  "notes": "USAGE: {抑圧|よくあつ} has both political/social and psychological meanings. In psychology, it refers to the unconscious pushing down of unacceptable thoughts or memories.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {感情|かんじょう}/{欲望|よくぼう}を{抑圧|よくあつ}する (to repress emotions/desires)\n- {抑圧|よくあつ}された{記憶|きおく} (repressed memories)\n- {抑圧|よくあつ}からの{解放|かいほう} (liberation from oppression)\n- {自由|じゆう}の{抑圧|よくあつ} (suppression of freedom)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {圧迫|あっぱく} (pressure, oppression - more physical)\n- {弾圧|だんあつ} (suppression, crackdown - political)\n- {抑制|よくせい} (restraint, control - less forceful)",
